=head2 create

  my $configuration = $client->intelligence->v3->configurations->create(\%body);

Create an Intelligence Configuration to control how and when language operators
analyze conversations. You must include the C<rules> field in the request. You
can pass an empty array (C<"rules": []>), but an Intelligence Configuration
with an empty C<rules> array doesn't execute any language operators. To add
rules later, make a C<PUT /v3/ControlPlane/Configurations/{id}> request. After
creating an Intelligence Configuration, you must attach it to a Conversations
Configuration by using the Conversations API. Returns a
C<ConfigurationInstance>.

